"""Render a standalone report from measured synthetic SMS benchmark results. No API calls."""
import argparse,json,html,re
from pathlib import Path
p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--input',type=Path,required=True);p.add_argument('--output',type=Path,required=True);args=p.parse_args()
data=json.loads(args.input.read_text());summary=data['summary'];total=summary['rules']['cases']
if data.get('errors') or any(s['cases']!=total for s in summary.values()):raise SystemExit('Benchmark incomplete; refusing to present a complete comparison')
source=(Path(__file__).parent/'run.ts').read_text();validator=source[source.index('function validate('):source.index('async function extract(')];extract=source[source.index('async function extract('):source.index('async function route(')]
labels={'rules':'Current parser','one_call':'One AI call','decision_then_extract':'Decide, then extract'}
rows='';bars=''
for key,s in summary.items():
 rows+=f'<tr><th>{labels[key]}</th><td>{s["otpExact"]}/{s["otpTotal"]}</td><td>{s["nonOtpFalsePositives"]}/{s["nonOtpTotal"]}</td><td>{s["categoryExact"] if s["categoryExact"] is not None else "Not supported"}</td><td>{s["medianMs"]/1000:.2f}s / {s["p95Ms"]/1000:.2f}s</td><td>${s["costUSD"]:.5f}</td></tr>'
 bars+=f'<div class="bar-row"><span>{labels[key]}</span><div class="track"><div class="bar" style="width:{100*s["codeExact"]/total}%"></div></div><strong>{s["codeExact"]}/{total}</strong></div>'
one=summary['one_call'];two=summary['decision_then_extract'];rule=summary['rules']
recommendation='Start with one AI call in observation mode.'
if one['nonOtpFalsePositives'] or one['wrongCodes']:recommendation='Keep AI in observation mode; wrong selections still need work.'
extra=f'One AI call found {one["otpExact"]} of {one["otpTotal"]} expected codes, versus {rule["otpExact"]} for the current parser. It returned a code for {one["nonOtpFalsePositives"]} messages that should have none.'
body='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>OTP Bridge — measured SMS benchmark</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:dark}body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;background:#10150f;color:#ecf2e7;max-width:1100px;margin:32px auto;padding:24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:38px}a{color:#d2f78c}p{max-width:90ch}.muted{color:#b4c2ad}.lead{padding:20px;background:#26331e;border-radius:12px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #485440}th{color:#d2f78c}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}.bar-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:180px 1fr 70px;gap:15px;margin:18px 0;align-items:center}.track{height:24px;background:#253120;border-radius:5px}.bar{height:100%;background:#c5ed82;border-radius:5px}select,button{font:inherit;padding:10px;border:1px solid #60734e;border-radius:6px;background:#202a1b;color:#eff8e6;margin:5px}pre{font:13px/1.6 ui-monospace,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#1c2518;padding:20px;border-radius:10px}.bad{color:#ffbfac}.good{color:#d2f78c}li{margin:8px 0}@media(max-width:650px){.bar-row{grid-template-columns:120px 1fr 55px;font-size:13px}body{padding:14px}h1{font-size:30px}}
</style><p class="muted">OTP BRIDGE · ACTUAL API BENCHMARK · SYNTHETIC SMS ONLY</p><h1>Can AI read the message<br>without guessing the code?</h1><div class="lead"><strong>RECOMMENDATION</strong><p>SUMMARY</p><p>EXTRA</p></div>
<p>This is a completed run of 60 hand-written synthetic messages across 11 categories. It compares the actual current parser, one GPT-6 Luna structured extraction call, and a Decisions classification call followed by extraction only for relevant categories. No real phone SMS, payment OTP, account balance or key was sent in a model prompt. Live capture, browser filling and payment settings were unchanged.</p>
<h2>Correct code or correct no-code result</h2>BARS<p class="muted">A success means the exact expected code, including leading zeroes, or null when no code should be selected. This does not measure browser autofill or payment completion.</p>
<h2>What each approach costs in time and money</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Approach</th><th>Valid codes found</th><th>False codes on non-code messages</th><th>Correct category / 60</th><th>Median / p95</th><th>Estimated run cost</th></tr>ROWS</table></div><p class="muted">Latency is local request-to-result time with concurrency three, excluding iPhone forwarding. The current parser runs locally and makes no API call. Cost is calculated from reported input, cached-input and output tokens at the linked standard model rates, not a billing receipt. The setup pilot and diagnostic requests are reported separately below.</p>
<h2>Bank fields and the remaining miss</h2><p>The one-call route matched 27 of 32 bank/merchant/amount/card fields exactly. All 32 matched after treating “ICICI” and “ICICI Bank” (likewise HDFC) as the same issuer. That alias audit was applied after the run; strict scores are preserved in the data. The remaining code miss was a literal letter-only login code whose text is CONFIDENTIAL. The model classified it as a login but returned no code.</p><p>The two-step route had one unresolved classification; it selected no code for that case. That counts as a missed code, not a successful result.</p><h2>Inspect any actual result</h2><select id="case"></select><label><input id="failures" type="checkbox"> Only cases with an error in any approach</label><p id="case-label"></p><pre id="message"></pre><div class="scroll"><table id="details"></table></div><p id="metadata"></p><p class="muted">These controls only inspect recorded synthetic results. They make no request and cannot read keys, messages or browser fields.</p>
<h2>Actual source: model output is checked against the SMS</h2><p>benchmarks/run.ts — the exact validation and request code used by this run:</p><pre>VALIDATOR</pre><p>The exact-substring check prevents inventing a code; the category and ambiguity checks suppress clearly irrelevant selections. These are benchmark checks, not proof that a selected code belongs to the active bank transaction.</p><pre>EXTRACT</pre><p>The request uses one fixed prompt and a strict field schema. The same prompt is used for both extraction paths, with reasoning effort disabled. It has no tools and cannot click, send, fetch a URL or inspect the key.</p>
<h2>What the results do not prove</h2><ul><li>The report JavaScript passed a syntax check. Browser automation could not inspect the local file because its URL policy blocks file URLs; the interactive controls have not been visually verified by the agent.</li><li>This is one run on 60 hand-written fixtures, not a random sample of your inbox or an independent holdout set. Exact percentages should not be read as future reliability.</li><li>The set includes masked cards, bank warnings, mixed/letter codes, leading zeroes, multiple codes, Hindi/Arabic/Chinese, receipts, coupons, personal messages and an instruction embedded in an SMS. Unsupported spaced-digit codes are expected to stay ambiguous.</li><li>The current parser does not classify general SMS or extract issuer/merchant/amount. Those features are evaluated separately for AI; they are not counted as parser classification failures.</li><li>Schema-valid AI output can still be wrong. A production version needs exact issuer/site/account binding, freshness, literal evidence checks and your saved action permissions.</li><li>The space trigger covers 59 of these 60 messages. The bare-code fixture has no space. This benchmark starts at message intake; it does not verify the installed iPhone Shortcut, forwarding coverage or phone delivery.</li><li>Both model routes are evaluated in fixed order, with shared prompts and possible warm-cache effects. p95 is from this small run and this machine/network.</li><li>Observation mode means collecting predictions without allowing those predictions to fill fields or trigger an automation. Any live AI rollout is a separate change.</li></ul><h2>Run record and next step</h2><p id="record"></p><p id="pilot"></p><p>Next: evaluate a new held-out synthetic set and shadow predictions before enabling AI-selected codes in the live extension. This experiment did not change phone forwarding or enable processing of real personal SMS by OpenAI.</p><p><a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/decisions">Decisions API</a> · <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs">Structured Outputs</a> · <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing">Model prices</a> · <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data">API data controls</a></p>
<script>const DATA=REPORT, LABELS=LABELJSON;const allIds=[...new Set(DATA.results.map(r=>r.id))];const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);function bad(id){return DATA.results.some(r=>r.id===id&&(!r.score.codeExact||(r.categorySupported&&!r.score.categoryExact)));}function choices(){const previous=$('case').value;$('case').replaceChildren();for(const id of allIds.filter(id=>!$('failures').checked||bad(id))){const opt=document.createElement('option');opt.value=id;opt.textContent=id;$('case').append(opt);}if([...$('case').options].some(o=>o.value===previous))$('case').value=previous;render();}function render(){const rows=DATA.results.filter(r=>r.id===$('case').value);if(!rows.length){$('message').textContent='No matching cases.';return;}const f=rows[0];$('case-label').textContent='Expected category: '+f.expectedCategory+' · Expected code: '+(f.expected.code??'none');$('message').textContent=f.text;const table=$('details');table.replaceChildren();const header=document.createElement('tr');for(const v of ['Approach','Selected code','Category','Code check','Time']){const th=document.createElement('th');th.textContent=v;header.append(th);}table.append(header);for(const row of rows){const tr=document.createElement('tr');for(const v of [LABELS[row.strategy],row.prediction.code??'none',row.prediction.category??'Not supported',row.score.codeExact?'Correct':'Wrong',(row.ms/1000).toFixed(2)+'s']){const td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=v;tr.append(td);}tr.className=row.score.codeExact?'good':'bad';table.append(tr);}const fields=Object.keys(f.expected).filter(k=>k!=='code');$('metadata').textContent=fields.length?'Expected extra fields: '+JSON.stringify(Object.fromEntries(fields.map(k=>[k,f.expected[k]])))+' · One-call result: '+JSON.stringify(rows.find(r=>r.strategy==='one_call')?.prediction):'No extra fields scored for this case.';}$('case').onchange=render;$('failures').onchange=choices;choices();$('record').textContent='Model: '+DATA.model+' · Started '+DATA.startedAt+' · Finished '+DATA.finishedAt+' · Fixture SHA-256: '+DATA.fixtureHash+' · Configuration SHA-256: '+DATA.configHash;$('pilot').textContent=DATA.pilot?'Separate one-case API pilot: '+DATA.pilot.calls+' calls, estimated $'+DATA.pilot.costUSD.toFixed(6)+'. Known diagnostic calls: '+(DATA.diagnostics?.callsWithUsage||0)+', estimated $'+(DATA.diagnostics?.costUSD||0).toFixed(6)+'. Total with reported token usage: $'+(DATA.pilot.costUSD+(DATA.diagnostics?.costUSD||0)+Object.values(DATA.summary).reduce((s,r)=>s+r.costUSD,0)).toFixed(6)+'. One earlier unresolved API call has no saved token usage and is excluded from this estimate.':'Pilot accounting not attached.';</script></html>'''
replacements={'SUMMARY':html.escape(recommendation),'EXTRA':html.escape(extra),'BARS':bars,'ROWS':rows,'VALIDATOR':html.escape(validator),'EXTRACT':html.escape(extract),'REPORT':json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False).replace('<','\\u003c'),'LABELJSON':json.dumps(labels)}
for key,value in sorted(replacements.items(),key=lambda x:len(x[0]),reverse=True):body=body.replace(key,value)
args.output.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);args.output.write_text(body)
print('Rendered measured benchmark report with recorded case inspection and actual source.')
